      "obligation": "refuter:19:1",
      "id": "lem-modified-pcp-reduces-to-pcp",
      "location": "Proof step 2.2",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 1.1 explicitly includes the copier tile \"$(*,*)$\". That tile alone is a nonempty ordinary-PCP match, since both concatenations are `*`. Thus step 2.2's assertion that \"any PCP match for the transformed instance must start with the unique tile whose top word begins with `#` and must end with the unique tile containing `$`\" is false. For example, modified-PCP instance $(a,b)$ has no match, but its transformed PCP instance has the one-tile copier match, so the claimed reduction equivalence fails.",
